Description: Thread placement for an appliance (DECKSMITHOS_AUDIO_CPUS)
 Linux only; without the variables nothing changes.
 DECKSMITHOS_AUDIO_CPUS="3": the PortAudio callback (engine) thread moves
 itself to these CPUs on its first callback; DecksmithOS keeps them free of
 everything else (systemd CPUAffinity, irqaffinity), so that the GUI, the
 waveforms, disk reads and other processes never delay the audio.
 DECKSMITHOS_BACKGROUND_NICE=10: track analysis and the library scan run
 with this nice value, below the GUI.
Author: DecksmithOS
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-11-22
